Assesses the synthetic datasets made in **PART 1 — Synthetic Data Generator** in two ways:

1. **Utility** (synthpop workflow, Raab, Nowok & Dibben): `utility.gen()` with a CART propensity model
   (VAE vs synthpop's own `syn()` as a benchmark), `compare()` one-way, `utility.tables()` two-way,
   `utility.tab()` per variable, ECDF / KS, and the same on a patient-level summary table
   (per-patient mean, SD, slope, days) so the longitudinal structure is tested too.
2. **Corsano daily models:** `Model4WearablesV2_DailyMeans()` from PART 4 is run unchanged on the original
   data, on each synthetic dataset and on bootstrap resamples of the original data (the ceiling: how much
   agreement is possible at all with 65 patients). Each run writes its usual Excel file, plots and GOF
   plots to its own folder. The results are then compared: BIC knot choice, bi-weekly estimated means,
   within-class change from baseline, Non-Responder − Responder contrasts and covariate effects.

